1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Starknet can hide who you are when you send money.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,500
Getting paid that way? Nothing exists.

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:13,000
No checkout. No invoice. Nothing to tell your server the money landed.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
So we built it.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,000
This arcade is the shop. No wallet, no install, it just runs.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,000
That panel is the whole widget. One call drops it into any page.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Drop a coin in.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The shop's server saw the payment and granted the credit. That's the loop.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,500
Now look at the price before you sign.

10
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:46,500
A one STRK coin costs seven.

11
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:54,000
The pool takes six every single time. Flat. Doesn't matter if you move one or a thousand.

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:01,000
That number is nowhere in STRK20's docs. We pulled it off the contract ourselves.

13
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Which means private payments have a floor. Under sixty STRK, fees eat more than ten percent.

14
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:16,000
This panel spells out what the payment leaks. Including the parts we couldn't hide.

15
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Merchant side. Every invoice gets a link and a QR.

16
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Or print one code and stick it on the counter. The customer picks the amount.

17
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,500
One printed code means one address forever. Anyone can add up your takings.

18
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:43,000
Your customers stay anonymous either way. We say so before you pick.

19
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The QR encoder is ours. No dependencies, checked against the ISO spec.

20
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Mainnet now. Real money.

21
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:02,000
See the warning? Nothing here has checked this link's amount or address, and it says so out loud.

22
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:08,000
A link can't vouch for itself, so we never let it try.

23
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:15,500
Signing. The pool submits it, so the chain never records me as the sender.

24
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:22,500
The merchant's watcher picks it up off public RPC. No wallet open anywhere.

25
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:30,000
It counts what came in, not what's sitting there. Money already on the address proves nothing.

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Signed webhook fires, the invoice flips to paid, and the order ships itself.

27
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Seven mainnet transactions. Over two hundred tests. Nine rounds of tearing it apart.

28
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:50,000
And the README says what those transactions don't prove, too.

29
00:02:50,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Stealth Checkout. The receiving side of STRK20. Code, docs and the transactions are all in the repo.
